Subject: Formula.service stores its block bound to Homebrew::Service

Formula#service passes the stored block to Homebrew::Service.new, whose initialize instance_evals it on the service, as
the service DSL's own parameter type already says: the stored and returned type now says so too.
---
diff --git a/Library/Homebrew/formula.rb b/Library/Homebrew/formula.rb
index 28ba83ad5f..46c9512f19 100644
--- a/Library/Homebrew/formula.rb
+++ b/Library/Homebrew/formula.rb
@@ -5095,13 +5095,13 @@ class Formula
       params(
         block: T.nilable(T.proc.bind(Homebrew::Service).void),
       ).returns(
-        T.nilable(T.proc.void),
+        T.nilable(T.proc.bind(Homebrew::Service).void),
       )
     }
     def service(&block)
       return @service_block unless block
 
-      @service_block = T.let(block, T.nilable(T.proc.void))
+      @service_block = T.let(block, T.nilable(T.proc.bind(Homebrew::Service).void))
     end
 
     # Defines whether the {Formula}'s bottle can be used on the given Homebrew
